WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.571
Welcome to the Seller University module.

00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:09.000
Today we'll discuss the generic product policy error code 5882 and how to address it.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.200
If you receive error code 5882, you may be attempting to create a generic product listing that has

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.000
been flagged as infringing on the intellectual property IP of a brand.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.200
Using another brand's IP in your generic product listing or listing a branded product as generic

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.000
violates Amazon's listing policies.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.533
To ensure compliance, first review the Amazon brand name policy and Amazon intellectual property

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:37.000
policy.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.545
If you believe you are following all policies and are still encountering this error code, click

00:00:43.545 --> 00:00:46.000
Help, then Get Help and Resources.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Select My Issue Is Not Listed and say I want to create a generic ASIN and receive error 5882.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.000
A member of Selling Partner Support will reach out to assist.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.647
Remember, maintaining the integrity of the Amazon Store is crucial for your success as a selling

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:05.000
partner.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store.
